{"id":"chatcmpl-c165bafe-6637-4369-8e0e-f88e4fd66dd1","object":"chat.completion","created":1795229692,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"When the imaging view is insufficient to directly assess the target finding (e.g., lateral view for coronal scoliosis laterality), the successful strategy was to triangulate multiple independent expert/model opinions and accept the consensus as the intended answer. The task also demonstrated adaptive re-querying with refined questions when initial evidence was ambiguous, and explicit risk acknowledgment before committing to an answer.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When the available view cannot directly reveal the finding, query multiple independent expert models and use their consensus as the decision signal.\",\n    \"If initial expert output is ambiguous or conflicts with the visual evidence, re-query with a more specific question targeting indirect signs rather than abandoning the finding.\",\n    \"Explicitly state the limitation of the evidence (e.g., view cannot show laterality) in the verification step, then justify the answer via model consensus and dataset-typical interpretation.\",\n    \"Use region-of-interest zooming to inspect the relevant anatomy directly before relying on model outputs, especially when the finding is subtle.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA with limited views\": \"When the image view cannot directly assess the asked property, gather 2+ independent model opinions and answer by consensus; note the limitation explicitly.\",\n    \"Ambiguous expert model outputs\": \"Re-query the expert with a refined, more specific question about indirect signs before finalizing; do not discard the first answer without a second probe.\",\n    \"Multi-model reconciliation\": \"Treat agreement between two independent VLMs as strong evidence, especially when direct visual confirmation is impossible.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm whether the image view can directly assess the asked property; if not, plan to triangulate via multiple model opinions.\",\n    \"Before answering, verify that at least two independent sources (models or visual cues) agree, and document the evidence limitation.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":781,"total_tokens":1171,"completion_tokens":390,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":781},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":390}}}